{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing Ruby install: add Ruby orb",
    "Explanation": [
      "The config contains only placeholders: '# Add Orb here' under orbs and '# Add step below to install Ruby version 2.6.3' in the steps. No actual install step exists, and the log shows only 'ruby -v' failing with 'command not found' (exit 127). So no installation was attempted. The config file is part of the 'koans-05-orbs' exercise, which points to the intended fix: declare the CircleCI Ruby orb (e.g., circleci/ruby) under orbs and add its ruby/install step with version '2.6.3' before 'ruby -v'. The other options are weaker fits. Changing the base image does not add an explicit install of 2.6.3. Installing via apt would not reliably provide exactly 2.6.3. Increasing the timeout does nothing for a missing binary."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
