{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Test results produced but not published",
    "Explanation": [
      "The `Run tests` step writes `~/project/results/test_results.xml` (a valid JUnit XML with one passing testcase). The log confirms this with \"Wrote ~/project/results/test_results.xml\", so results are produced.",
      "",
      "The step then runs `exit 1`. The log shows \"Exited with code exit status 1\" and \"CircleCI received exit code 1\", so the job is red, not green.",
      "",
      "The config has no `store_test_results` step, so nothing reaches the Tests (test summary) tab. It also has no `store_artifacts` step, so the file is not kept as an artifact. Both publication steps are missing.",
      "",
      "The fix is to add both steps pointing at the results path, for example `store_test_results: path: ~/project/results` and `store_artifacts: path: ~/project/results/test_results.xml`. The run step ends with `exit 1`, and steps run only on success by default. So these steps should use `when: always` to still run after the failure.",
      "",
      "Removing `exit 1` alone would turn the job green but still publish nothing. Adding only one of the two steps would meet only half of the requirement. `set_upload_true` is not a real publication mechanism here."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
      "  \"job_green\": false,",
      "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
      "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
      "  \"results_produced\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_store_test_results_and_store_artifacts\",",
        "  \"job_green\": false,",
        "  \"missing_store_artifacts\": true,",
        "  \"missing_store_test_results\": true,",
        "  \"results_produced\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
