{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy job lacks production branch filter",
    "Explanation": [
      "The config places no branch filter on the deploy job. When a workflow job entry has no `filters.branches` key, CircleCI runs it on every branch. The observed pipeline #151 ran on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`. Every job succeeded, including deploy, so the pipeline is green. The requirement is still violated, because deploy ran on a non-production branch.",
      "",
      "The `requires` chain (deploy requires test-production, which requires build) only controls the order jobs run in. It does not restrict which branches a job runs on.",
      "",
      "Branch eligibility is controlled at the workflow level, on the deploy job's entry under `workflows.build-test-and-deploy.jobs`. The fix is to add `filters: branches: only: production` there. Filters cannot be placed on the job definition under the top-level `jobs:` key. A `branches.ignore` list of non-production branches would be fragile, and relying on `requires` does nothing for branch filtering. Only deploy needs the filter; build and test-production can keep running on all branches."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
