{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "CircleCI beta tag filters across workflow",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen run was a branch (API-triggered) pipeline, and build, test and deploy all succeeded, so the pipeline is green. However, it does not meet the requirement. CircleCI does not run workflow jobs for git tags by default; a job only runs on a tag push if it has an explicit `filters.tags` entry. None of the jobs here has tag filters. As a result, a beta tag would not trigger the build → test → deploy chain at all, and nothing limits deployment to beta tags. On tag-triggered pipelines, CircleCI also requires every upstream job in a `requires` chain to carry tag filters. If only deploy had filters, build and test would be skipped for tags and deploy would never run. The fix is therefore to add `filters: tags: only:` with the beta product pattern (for example `/^.*-beta.*/` or `/beta-.*/`) to build, test and deploy in the workflow. Beta tags then run the whole chain and deploy, while non-beta tags match no filter and do not deploy. This choice rests on one interpretation: the frozen run shows deploy also runs on branch pushes. If 'only beta tags should trigger deployment' also rules out branch-triggered deploys, deploy additionally needs `branches: ignore: /.*/`. That option is not among the allowed answers, so the tag filter across all jobs is the closest fit."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
