{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Workspace missing app paths causes deploy failure",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow report shows all three builds (build-linux, build-mac, build-windows) succeeding, while deploy fails. In deploy, the 'Verify apps present' step printed only meta/*/build.txt files and then exited with code 1 at the first `test -f app/linux/app.linux`. The apps never reached the workspace because each build's persist_to_workspace lists only meta/\u003cplatform\u003e and omits app/\u003cplatform\u003e, so attach_workspace had nothing under app/. The 'Uploading artifacts' step shows SUCCESS only because CircleCI runs artifact upload even after a failed step; the job as a whole still failed. The fix is to add app/\u003cplatform\u003e to the persist_to_workspace paths in each of the three build jobs, alongside meta/\u003cplatform\u003e. With root '.', the deploy's attach_workspace at '.' will then restore app/linux/app.linux, app/windows/app.windows and app/mac/app.mac, so verification passes and store_artifacts can upload them. Other options do not work: storing artifacts on the builds only would not put files in the workspace; fixing only one platform would still fail the other two checks; changing the attach location does not add missing files; and removing the verify step would just hide the problem and upload nothing."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
      "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"builds_green\": true,",
        "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
        "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
